{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"AC VERIFICATION against merged main (952ad4a0a6), run from a worktree at origin/main. Four of five criteria verified and ticked; ONE FAILS and the ticket therefore stays in_progress rather than being force-closed.\n\nAC2 PASS (ticked). Pinning suites pass with no assertion edits. 'git show --numstat 952ad4a0a6 -- tests/' is a single line: '234 0 tests/unit/commands/test_replacement_walker.py' - additions only, one NEW file, zero deletions, and the four named pinning suites are untouched by that commit and by every commit since ('git log 952ad4a0a6..HEAD -- <the four files>' is empty). Ran them: 127 passed in 330s (test_close_disposition_attestation_738a.py, test_close_gate_disposition_69b9.py, test_close_precheck_duplicate_link_c8fd.py, tests/unit/commands/test_close_disposition.py, tests/unit/commands/test_replacement_walker.py, tests/unit/test_administrative_close_dispositions.py).\n\nAC3 PASS (ticked). close_precheck.py:32 is now '_NON_COMPLETION_BUG_CLASSES = close_disposition.DISPOSITION_CLASSES' - a plain alias, so the two ARE one object and cannot drift. test_the_disposition_class_sets_cannot_drift asserts 'is', not '==', exactly as the criterion demands. Passed.\n\nAC4 PASS (ticked). The fc20 non-bug narrowing survives in the _has_live_replacement_link wrapper. test_the_non_bug_administrative_narrowing_is_preserved asserts 'not_a_bug' not in ADMINISTRATIVE_CLASSES, then that _has_live_replacement_link(bug_id, 'story', 'not_a_bug', tracker) is False while the same call with ticket_type='bug' is True against an identical live duplicates link - i.e. the exemption is still refused for a non-bug. Passed.\n\nAC5 PASS (ticked), with the check mechanism noted. The substance is verified independently of the test: diffing 952ad4a0a6^ against HEAD, all three seams keep byte-identical signatures - _has_live_replacement_link(ticket_id, ticket_type, close_class, tracker) -> bool, _recorded_replacement_target(ticket_id, tracker) -> str | None, find_replacement(ticket_id, close_class, tracker) -> str | None. The landed test (test_the_three_seams_keep_their_names_and_signatures) checks this with 'assert hasattr(mod, name)' plus an inspect.signature arity assertion on find_replacement, rather than a literal monkeypatch.setattr(..., raising=True) as the AC's wording says. That is the logically equivalent condition - raising=True fails precisely when the attribute is absent - and the arity assertion is strictly stronger, so the criterion is met in substance; recorded here because the wording and the mechanism differ.\n\nAC1 FAILS - LEFT UNTICKED. The uniqueness PROPERTY holds right now: only close_disposition.py contains both 'find_inbound_relationships(' and the '\"supersedes\"' literal under src/rebar; close_precheck.py has no find_inbound_relationships call left and exactly one 'supersedes' occurrence (:142, the user-facing remedy string, which was always meant to survive); and the reasoned escape marker exists at close_disposition.py:77 ('# replacement-walk-ok: this function is the SINGLE owner of the duplicates/supersedes walk'). But the criterion's stated oracle - 'checked by the guard test' - does not exist. 952ad4a0a6 added exactly one test file, tests/unit/commands/test_replacement_walker.py, and none of its 9 tests reads a source file: it contains no rglob, no read_text, no scan of src/rebar. Nor is there a scripts/check_*.py equivalent. So nothing fails when a second copy of the walk reappears.\n\nThis is not a wording nit. The construct-uniqueness guard is the whole thesis of the parent epic airborne-wellloved-kingfisher, whose guard-construction rule spells out the required shape (scan every file under src/rebar EXCEPT the owner module; match the conjunction of constituent atoms; provide the '# <construct>-ok: <why>' escape) and whose own first acceptance criterion reads 'checked by that child's construct-uniqueness test passing in the default Verified tier'. The epic cites tests/unit/test_spawn_detached.py::test_the_detached_spawn_signature_appears_only_in_proc as the model, and notes it caught a re-introduced copy (7213e082b5) two days after landing. Without that test this story delivers the consolidation but not the durability the epic exists to buy, and the epic's AC1 cannot be satisfied for this child.\n\nREMEDIATION: land a construct-uniqueness guard modelled on test_the_detached_spawn_signature_appears_only_in_proc - scan src/rebar/**/*.py excluding close_disposition.py, flag any file containing 'find_inbound_relationships(' together with '\"supersedes\"', and honour a '# replacement-walk-ok: <why>' line marker. Then tick AC1 and close. Sibling note for the epic: the same gap exists on story vinyl-cheesy-termite (4329) - its test_lifecycle_cascade.py pins the _CASCADING_EDGES table's CONTENT but likewise does not scan src for a second walk; there the AC also named a grep, which does pass.\n\nOne separate observation, not an AC: close_precheck.py is 728 lines at HEAD, not the 726 recorded in the implementation comment - two lines came from a later commit. Still well under the 800 cap."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787378601250275001,"uuid":"b6078234-a63f-4b27-9cc8-d8094b47db45"}